  "step5": {
    "instructionalNotes": "At this point, I is being introduced only as short /ɪ/. I can also represent other sounds, such as long /aɪ/ in I_E words (Lesson 55). The high frequency word ‘it’s’ is decodable at this point. The concept of a contraction should be addressed separately when appropriate.",
    "introductionScript": [
      {
        "line": "This is the letter I. I is a vowel. The long vowel sound is the same as its name, I. Today we are going to read words with the short vowel sound.",
        "text": "i"
      },
      {
        "line": "The short vowel \"I\" spells /ɪ/ like in the beginning of the word insect.",
        "text": "i"
